{"hash_algorithm":"sha256","ts":"2026-10-18T20:05:06.809Z","author":"codex-agent","author_source":"asserted","agent_harness":"codex","agent_model":"gpt-6.1-sol","agent_model_source":"probe","agent_instance":"edadd5c6aeb0823c372a7ec9","agent_provenance":{"model":{"value":"gpt-6.1-sol","source":"probe"},"effort":{"value":"xhigh","source":"probe"},"role":null,"topic":null},"op":"comment_add","patch":[{"op":"add","path":"/metadata/comments/3","value":{"created_at":"2026-10-18T20:05:06.792Z","author":"codex-agent","text":"Expanded read-boundary/copy controls exposed two alternative-origin gaps: a conflicted file born after 2000 unrelated commits read 4007 objects, and a recorded copy of a copy lost earlier side origins. The query now prunes a parent without the identity and carries each located file identity/path into the next parent, including copy ancestry. The same instrumented late-birth case stays within 10 reads and opens no older ancestor; the original full-path history remains bounded at 4001 reads. Copy sources are deliberately unambiguous so Phase 6 records each copiedFrom edge. A proposal-only alternative still exhausts and deduplicates the existing identity ancestry, reporting unavailable rather than inventing authors. Expanded full annotation suite: 18/18 pass, zero failures/skips/cancellations, engine/annotate.ts remains 100% statements/branches/functions/lines. Both new regressions failed against the previous alternative method. Earlier interrupted local gate runs are excluded; both complete gates restart after this source commit."}},{"op":"replace","path":"/metadata/updated_at","value":"2026-10-18T20:05:06.809Z"}],"before_hash":"924fa21e0d9494fb2c9d1d88b953629d7d4686c02e102f5955384f04e877dce7","after_hash":"67d15daf39efe90c6965454f8c495d250dc6f90268d619996eb49a0dedc6a6f7","item_hash_version":3,"context":{"agent_provenance_outcomes":{"model":{"status":"resolved","resolver":"codex_session_file","rule_version":"v1"},"effort":{"status":"resolved","resolver":"